Subject: [PATCH] modsign: ask for the authority key identifier always

The kernel signs its modules with a key pair it makes at build time, and loads the
certificate at boot. This kernel accepts a certificate only if it has both the
subject and the authority key identifier
(crypto/asymmetric_keys/x509_public_key.c). The request written to x509.genkey says
"authorityKeyIdentifier=keyid", and a current OpenSSL (3.5.7 where this was seen)
leaves that extension out of a self-signed certificate unless it is told "always".
Every boot then logs

    X.509: Cert for 'Magrathea: Glacier signing key' must have SubjKeyId and AuthKeyId extensions
    Problem loading in-kernel X.509 certificate (-129)

and with CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE no module can be loaded, signed or not.

An output directory that already has x509.genkey and signing_key.* keeps them: they
have to be removed for the new request to be used.
---
--- kernel/Makefile
+++ kernel/Makefile
@@ -214,5 +214,5 @@
 	@echo >>x509.genkey "basicConstraints=critical,CA:FALSE"
 	@echo >>x509.genkey "keyUsage=digitalSignature"
 	@echo >>x509.genkey "subjectKeyIdentifier=hash"
-	@echo >>x509.genkey "authorityKeyIdentifier=keyid"
+	@echo >>x509.genkey "authorityKeyIdentifier=keyid:always"
 endif
